
db.createCollection("orders", {
  validator: {
    $jsonSchema: {
      bsonType: "object",
      required: ["orderId", "customerName", "items", "totalAmount", "createdAt"],
      properties: {
        orderId: {
          bsonType: "string",
          description: "must be a string and is required"
        },
        customerName: {
          bsonType: "string",
          minLength: 1,
          description: "must be a non-empty string"
        },
        items: {
          bsonType: "array",
          minItems: 1,
          items: {
            bsonType: "object",
            required: ["productId", "quantity", "price"],
            properties: {
              productId: {
                bsonType: "string",
                description: "must be a string"
              },
              quantity: {
                bsonType: "int",
                minimum: 1,
                description: "must be an integer >= 1"
              },
              price: {
                bsonType: "double",
                minimum: 0,
                description: "must be a non-negative number"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        totalAmount: {
          bsonType: "double",
          minimum: 0,
          description: "must be a non-negative number"
        },
        status: {
          enum: ["Pending", "Shipped", "Completed", "Cancelled"],
          description: "can only be one of the enum values"
        },
        createdAt: {
          bsonType: "date",
          description: "must be a valid date"
        }
      }
    }
  },
  validationLevel: "strict",   // (off / moderate / strict)
  validationAction: "error"    // (warn / error)
});

Notes : In details here in this case: 
-------------------------------------------- >
$jsonSchema → defines rules for documents.

required → enforces mandatory fields.

bsonType → MongoDB types (string, int, double, date, object, array, etc.).

enum → restricts values to a fixed set.

validationLevel: 
strict → validates all inserts/updates.
moderate → validates only inserts and updates that already have valid schema.

validationAction:
error → rejects invalid docs.
warn → logs a warning but allows invalid docs.

